            <ArticleTitle>[Gastrointestinal manifestation of Recklinghausen's disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>375-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1556/MOnkol.52.2008.4.6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a 52-year-old women suffering in Recklinghausen's disease, operated for acute abdomen, subserous neurinomas and neurofibroma were found on the jejunum and in the mesentery. Gastrointestinal tumors (neurofibroma, GIST, carcinoid etc.) should be considered in patients with Recklinghausen's disease and gastrointestinal symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
